## TaskJoinFuture — joins a spawned task.
##
## v1 user surface: hand-poll, NOT `.await`. Constructed by
## `Task.join(handle)`; polled directly via
## `(&var join).poll(&var cx)` and matched on the `Poll[Int]`
## result. See the 728 e2e fixture for the canonical shape.
##
## Why not `.await`: async-lowering's class-static-method awaitee
## desugar (commit 8bab0e2) resolves the awaitee's Future class
## via `collect_future_outputs`, which walks only the user-program
## AST. TaskJoinFuture lives in bootstrap-loaded stdlib and is
## invisible to that walker today. Same gap defers
## `731_class_static_call_await.rvn.deferred`. When the
## architectural fix lands (making lower_async_defs see bootstrap
## classes), `Task.join(h).await` works with zero changes to this
## file.
##
## Spec docs/specs/stdlib/task_spawn.spec.md §B4. Polling:
##   - If `TaskHandle.is_done(handle) == 1`: Ready(result).
##   - Else: Pending.
##
## The result is the i64 stored by the C-side scheduler when the
## spawned task completed (the payload of `Poll.Ready` from that
## task's final poll). For v1, the join future's Output is `Int` —
## generic-T recovery requires either typed lib decls or a typeck-
## time substitution pass; both are deferred to the multi-threaded
## scheduler round. Callers wanting typed results pay the cost of
## an Int → T cast at the use site.
##
## Drop semantics: `def drop` decrements the caller-side handle
## refcount (regardless of whether the task ever completed). This
## means leaving an un-awaited join future is safe — the handle's
## queue-side ref stays live, the task continues to completion or
## drain, and the caller-side ref drops cleanly here. The
## TaskHandle static-method namespace's `drop_handle` is for raw-
## Int handle ops; this `def drop` is the future-class hook the
## state machine fires when the join future falls out of scope.
class TaskJoinFuture
  handle: Int
  include Future
  type Output = Int

  def init(h: Int)
    self.handle = h
  end

  def var poll(cx: &var Context) -> Poll[Int]
    if TaskHandle.is_done(self.handle) == 1
      Poll.Ready(TaskHandle.result(self.handle))
    else
      Poll.Pending
    end
  end

  def drop
    TaskHandle.drop_handle(self.handle)
  end
end
